Z||000001||Shiner||11-14-2000||11:45 PM||||88,<P> Yep, I was thinking the same.  I am planning on getting the same one in about a month.  I hate how the single DIN recievers look with an adapter, and this radio is about the only good one in the 1.5 DIN size.  <P> Just remember, it's 45 watts PEAK, not constant.  I think it's like 20 or 22 watts RMS.  Still a decent amount of power.  And as long as it sounds good, you can always add an external amp.<P> Here's to our good taste!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Shiner-<BR>'84 Sport Coupe<BR>'87 GT<BR>'86 SE 2M6 (parts car)||||reg||1
