Z||000013||batboy||11-15-2000||10:54 PM||||I have the older model Pioneer DEH45 and love it. It might not be as powerful or as fancy as the newer ones, but it was a great price. There are two models of Alpine CD players out now that will fit too. Close to $400 for the cheaper Alpine. The expensive model has 4 volt pre-outs.<P>Bam, a DIN sized head unit is the "standard" size. Our Fieros take a 1.5 DIN which are bigger. Was that what you were asking?||||reg||1
Z||000014||286SE'S||11-16-2000||03:19 PM||||They are nice. I have a DEH-76DH and its been<BR>great. Been in the car for three years and never skipped once. Has anyone else had a problem with the AM band in these Pioneers being totally worthless when the engine is running? Not that I actually listen to AM but noticed it was just static/whine one day stuck in traffic and trying to see if there was a reason for the jam.||||reg||1
